{
  "_comment": "Chinese text-to-image. Chroma's T5 encoder cannot read Chinese — a Chinese prompt returns something unrelated to what was asked while still costing credits — but Qwen-Image-Edit reads it natively, which is already proven by img2img. This is that same graph with the uploaded photo replaced by a blank canvas, so there is nothing to preserve and the whole frame is repainted from the description. No new weights, no extra cold start: it runs on the worker that is already deployed.",
